.TH "cog" "1" "2026-06-26"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
cog - deterministic helper CLI for agent-oriented development workflows
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBcog\fR [\fB-h\fR|\fB--help\fR] [\fB-V\fR|\fB--version\fR] [\fB--json\fR] [\fB--dry-run\fR] [\fB--print-config\fR] [\fB-v\fR|\fB-vv\fR|\fB-vvv\fR] <command> [args]
.PP
\fBcog help\fR [command]
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBcog\fR is a Bash CLI that provides deterministic helper commands for
agent-oriented development workflows.\& It is installed as a self-contained app
root containing its executable shim, libraries, templates, and version file.\&
.PP
The command list and short descriptions are sourced from command modules under
\fBlib/commands\fR.\& Each command module declares its summary with a line-2
\fBdesc:\fR sentinel.\&
.PP
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.PP
\fB-h\fR, \fB--help\fR
.RS 4
Show help for cog or for the selected command.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB-V\fR, \fB--version\fR
.RS 4
Print the cog version.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--json\fR
.RS 4
Request machine-readable output from commands that support it.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--dry-run\fR
.RS 4
Show what would happen without changing state where supported.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB--print-config\fR
.RS 4
Print resolved configuration values and their sources.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB-v\fR, \fB-vv\fR, \fB-vvv\fR
.RS 4
Increase verbosity.\&
.PP
.RE
